Argyle was a tall man in [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] who smelled of frankincense and myrrh, wore armor, and carried a shield. He was a trained healer, and was a contact of [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]] in [[Org/The Scale/index|the Scale]].

He was killed in the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and his soul did not return with the others; the Party dreamed of it chained between a light pulling up and a dark pulling down.

His axe, shield, grappling gun, cigarettes, business cards and gold were kept in the armory of the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] with the gear the gang had stripped from the dead. The Party recovered them there.

Argyle came back from the dead. He says the [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Judge of Ages|Judge]] ripped him from perdition and set him back in the same body, a little taller and with different eyes, his raiment twice the size it had been. He is closer to the Judge now and carries less of another influence, which he will not name. Only part of him returned: he calls the rest a philosophical perdition. He is looking for the other half, which he understands went voidward, and says the halves were bonded and are meant to be bonded. The other half is also part of the Judge, he does not mean to kill it, and anyone who sees another Argyle should tell him at once, since it is likely a demon wearing his face.

He came into the [[Sin and Tonic]] while the others were eating and greeted them as compatriots. They did not take him at his word: he talked like an officer of the [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]], and when [[People/Benny|Benny]] resonated at him the answer came back faint. He said he was cleared to not charge them with any crimes, and asked to be called Dr. Argyle, FFCS, apprentice timekeeper. [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] wanted him tested on a dangerous job, and the Party settled on having everyone checked for demonic presence by a diabolist.

Before he left for the bar he was briefed in a smoke-filled room by [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]], who is folded out of paper, and by the goat-legged fiend [[Divinity/Fiends/Flintlock Toboggan|Flintlock]], who told him his old friends were headed voidward, advised him to bunk up with them, and told him not to die this time.

The [[People/Sharp the Cunning Man|Cunning Man]] checked him and found no demon or devil in him, only the same tenuous settling in his own body that [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] has. Cleared, he rejoined the others. He says the half of him that went voidward is part of the [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Judge of Ages|Judge]] too, he means to find it and re-merge rather than kill it, and he does not know how. His business cards were made new and the old ones thrown in the river with most of his possessions. He asked whether the men who dumped him in the river died with honor; [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] did not, and the rest went down in a good fight.

He took up free medicine for people who cannot pay, working as a back-alley surgeon. He converted his gold into small jewels rather than trust the money system. He told the others he was staying in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] with the others rather than going on the pilgrimage.
